statement:
Retain one common canonical hard-branch instantiation of accepted facts 036a276c54ec5e66, 0b93509e5294c8fe, 2fe46f47d19112ea, 8788f2abe00654ed, and their cited accepted predecessors. Thus \(n,d\in\mathbb Z_{>0}\), \(C\subseteq\mathbb R^n\times\mathbb R^d\) is a convex body,
\[
 C_z:=\{x\in\mathbb R^d:(z,x)\in C\},
 \qquad
 a_z:=\operatorname{vol}_d(C_z),
 \qquad
 \gamma_d:=\left(\frac d{d+1}\right)^d,
\tag{1}
\]
and \(Q>0\) is the mass of the half-strength canonical product reservoir. Put
\[
 G:=\mathfrak C_{\rm core}(C),
 \qquad
 D:=2^nh_{\max}(C).
\tag{2}
\]
The hard ledger gives
\[
 G+R_{\rm sel}(C)+D<\frac Q{100}.
\tag{3}
\]

Let \(\Sigma\) be the complete positive label set of one actual maximum transverse pairing from accepted fact 036a276c54ec5e66. A label is
\[
 \sigma=(z(\sigma);e_\sigma,f_\sigma),
 \qquad
 e_\sigma\ne f_\sigma,
 \qquad
 \theta_\sigma>0,
\tag{4}
\]
where the two original reservoir parent edges share the anchor \(z(\sigma)\). Write \(P:=\sum_{\sigma\in\Sigma}\theta_\sigma\). Then
\[
 P>\frac{99Q}{200}.
\tag{5}
\]
For every original positive-load reservoir edge \(g=\{u,v\}\), retain its load \(\omega_g\), endpoint contacts
\[
 x_{g,u}\in\mathsf M_{a_u/2}(C_u),
 \qquad
 x_{g,v}\in\mathsf M_{a_v/2}(C_v),
\tag{6}
\]
their fixed half-mass witness densities \(f_{g,u},f_{g,v}\), and
\[
 m_g:=\frac{u+v}{2},
 \qquad
 \ell_g:=\frac{x_{g,u}+x_{g,v}}2
\tag{7}
\]

The common-midpoint whole-label family \(\mathscr B\) of accepted facts 0b93509e5294c8fe and 8788f2abe00654ed is a subfamily of the rescaled internal atlas. In particular, it is contained in the complete internal family
\[
 \mathscr A_{\rm int}\subseteq\Sigma,
 \qquad
 0<\eta_\sigma\leq\theta_\sigma,
 \qquad
 H_{\rm int}:=\sum_{\sigma\in\mathscr A_{\rm int}}\eta_\sigma
 >\frac{7Q}{400}.
\tag{8}
\]

The following completion theorem applies simultaneously to either specialization in (36). More generally, let \(\varnothing\ne\mathscr F\subseteq\Sigma\), choose weights
\[
 0<\lambda_\sigma\leq\theta_\sigma
 \qquad(\sigma\in\mathscr F),
 \qquad
 L:=\sum_{\sigma\in\mathscr F}\lambda_\sigma,
\tag{9}
\]
and retain each label's two actual original parent edges. For an original edge \(g\) and an anchor \(z\), put
\[
 \kappa_g:=
 \sum_{\substack{\sigma\in\mathscr F:\\
 g\in\{e_\sigma,f_\sigma\}}}\lambda_\sigma,
 \qquad
 b_{g,z}:=
 \sum_{\substack{\sigma\in\mathscr F:\ z(\sigma)=z,\\
 g\in\{e_\sigma,f_\sigma\}}}\lambda_\sigma,
\tag{10}
\]
and define
\[
 Z_{\mathscr F}:=\{z(\sigma):\sigma\in\mathscr F\},
 \qquad
 L_z:=\sum_{\substack{\sigma\in\mathscr F:\ z(\sigma)=z}}
 \lambda_\sigma.
\tag{11}
\]
Then the exact original-pairing ledger is
\[
 \boxed{0\leq\kappa_g\leq\omega_g,}
 \qquad
 \boxed{\sum_g\kappa_g=2L,}
\tag{12}
\]
\[
 \boxed{\sum_{g\ni z}b_{g,z}=2L_z,}
 \qquad
 \boxed{L_z\leq\frac{a_z}{8}
 <\frac{Q}{800\,2^n}.}
\tag{13}
\]

Every charged original parent pair is completed at its actual integer midpoint:
\[
 \boxed{\ell_g\in\mathsf M_{\kappa_g}(C_{m_g})
 \qquad(\kappa_g>0).}
\tag{14}
\]
The single measure
\[
 \nu_{\rm par}^{\mathscr F}
 :=2\gamma_d\sum_{g:\kappa_g>0}
 \kappa_g\delta_{(m_g,\ell_g)}
\tag{15}
\]
is carried by \(C\cap(\mathbb Z^n\times\mathbb R^d)\), is halfspace-dominated by the mixed-volume measure \(\mu_C\), and has exact mass
\[
 \boxed{|\nu_{\rm par}^{\mathscr F}|=4\gamma_dL.}
\tag{16}
\]

All anchor-side occurrences can also be pooled without loss. There are points \(p_z\in C_z\), one for every \(z\in Z_{\mathscr F}\), such that
\[
 \boxed{p_z\in\mathsf M_{4L_z}(C_z),}
 \qquad
 \boxed{\delta_C(z,p_z)\geq4\gamma_dL_z.}
\tag{17}
\]
Consequently
\[
 \nu_{\rm anc}^{\mathscr F}
 :=4\gamma_d\sum_{z\in Z_{\mathscr F}}
 L_z\delta_{(z,p_z)}
\tag{18}
\]
is carried by the mixed lattice section, is halfspace-dominated by \(\mu_C\), and has exact mass
\[
 \boxed{|\nu_{\rm anc}^{\mathscr F}|=4\gamma_dL.}
\tag{19}
\]

For every parity class \(\xi\in(\mathbb Z/2\mathbb Z)^n\), put
\[
 L_\xi:=\sum_{\substack{z\in Z_{\mathscr F}\\
 z\equiv\xi\ ({\rm mod}\ 2)}}L_z.
\tag{20}
\]
On every unordered pair of distinct anchors in one nonempty parity class define the complete product matching
\[
 q_{uv}^{\mathscr F}:=
 \frac{2L_uL_v}{L_\xi}
 \qquad
 (u\ne v,\ u\equiv v\equiv\xi,\ L_\xi>0),
\tag{21}
\]
and put it equal to zero on all other pairs. It is a free same-parity matching with
\[
 \boxed{
 d_u(q^{\mathscr F})
 =2L_u\left(1-\frac{L_u}{L_\xi}\right)
 \leq2L_u\leq\frac{a_u}{4}.}
\tag{22}
\]
Its mass is
\[
 \Lambda_{\mathscr F}:=|q^{\mathscr F}|
 =L-
 \sum_{\xi:L_\xi>0}
 \frac{\sum_{z\equiv\xi}L_z^2}{L_\xi},
\tag{23}
\]
and the collision-independent atom cap in (13) gives
\[
 \boxed{\Lambda_{\mathscr F}>L-\frac Q{800}.}
\tag{24}
\]

For every edge \(\{u,v\}\) of \(q^{\mathscr F}\), put
\[
 m_{uv}:=\frac{u+v}{2}\in\mathbb Z^n,
 \qquad
 x_{uv}:=\frac{p_u+p_v}{2}
\tag{25}
\]
Then every convexity-forced anchor midpoint is retained:
\[
 \boxed{
 \frac{C_u+C_v}{2}\subseteq C_{m_{uv}},
 \qquad
 x_{uv}\in\mathsf M_{q_{uv}^{\mathscr F}}(C_{m_{uv}}).}
\tag{26}
\]
The single off-diagonal product-midpoint measure
\[
 \nu_{\rm mid}^{\mathscr F}
 :=2\gamma_d
 \sum_{\{u,v\}:q_{uv}^{\mathscr F}>0}
 q_{uv}^{\mathscr F}
 \delta_{(m_{uv},x_{uv})}
\tag{27}
\]
is carried by the mixed lattice section, is halfspace-dominated by \(\mu_C\), and remains so after every coincident base or full atom is aggregated. Its exact mass is
\[
 \boxed{|\nu_{\rm mid}^{\mathscr F}|
 =2\gamma_d\Lambda_{\mathscr F}.}
\tag{28}
\]

For \(*\in\{\mathrm{par},\mathrm{anc},\mathrm{mid}\}\), let \((\rho_*^{\mathscr F},r_*^{\mathscr F})\) be the intrinsic base and continuous residual ranks of \(\nu_*^{\mathscr F}\), after physical atoms are aggregated. When \(\Lambda_{\mathscr F}>0\), the exact capacity conclusions are
\[
 \boxed{
 D\geq
 4\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_{\rm par}^{\mathscr F}}
 \frac{L}{r_{\rm par}^{\mathscr F}+1},}
\tag{29}
\]
\[
 \boxed{
 D\geq S_{\rm anc}^{\mathscr F},
 \qquad
 R_{\rm sel}(C)\geq S_{\rm anc}^{\mathscr F},
 \qquad
 S_{\rm anc}^{\mathscr F}:=
 4\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_{\rm anc}^{\mathscr F}}
 \frac{L}{r_{\rm anc}^{\mathscr F}+1},}
\tag{30}
\]
\[
 \boxed{
 D\geq
 2\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_{\rm mid}^{\mathscr F}}
 \frac{\Lambda_{\mathscr F}}
 {r_{\rm mid}^{\mathscr F}+1}.}
\tag{31}
\]
If \(r_{\rm anc}^{\mathscr F}=0\), then the pooled anchor points lie on one affine map and
\[
 \boxed{G\geq4L.}
\tag{32}
\]
Under the hard ledger, (29)--(31) instead force
\[
 \boxed{
 r_{\rm par}^{\mathscr F}+1
 >400\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_{\rm par}^{\mathscr F}}
 \frac LQ,}
\tag{33}
\]
\[
 \boxed{
 r_{\rm anc}^{\mathscr F}+1
 >800\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_{\rm anc}^{\mathscr F}}
 \frac LQ,}
\tag{34}
\]
\[
 \boxed{
 r_{\rm mid}^{\mathscr F}+1
 >200\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_{\rm mid}^{\mathscr F}}
 \frac{\Lambda_{\mathscr F}}Q.}
\tag{35}
\]

The two mandatory specializations are
\[
 \begin{array}{c|c|c}
 \mathscr F&\lambda_\sigma&L\\ \hline
 \Sigma&\theta_\sigma&P>99Q/200\\
 \mathscr A_{\rm int}&\eta_\sigma&H_{\rm int}>7Q/400.
 \end{array}
\tag{36}
\]
For the full maximum pairing,
\[
 \boxed{|Z_\Sigma|>396\,2^n,}
 \qquad
 \boxed{\Lambda_\Sigma>\frac{79Q}{160},}
\tag{37}
\]
and (33)--(35) sharpen to
\[
 r_{\rm par}^{\Sigma}+1
 >198\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_{\rm par}^{\Sigma}},
 \qquad
 r_{\rm anc}^{\Sigma}+1
 >396\gamma_d2^{n-\rho_{\rm anc}^{\Sigma}},
\tag{38}
\]
\[
 r_{\rm mid}^{\Sigma}+1
 >\frac{395}{4}\gamma_d
 2^{n-\rho_{\rm mid}^{\Sigma}}.
\tag{39}
\]
For the complete rescaled internal atlas, which contains \(\mathscr B\) and every auxiliary rescaled internal label,
\[
 \boxed{|Z_{\mathscr A_{\rm int}}|>14\,2^n,}
 \qquad
 \boxed{\Lambda_{\mathscr A_{\rm int}}
 >\frac{13Q}{800}.}
\tag{40}
\]

Finally apply the accepted hereditary matching tower to the two complete product matchings. Since accepted fact 2fe46f47d19112ea gives \(\gamma_d>4/11\),
\[
 4\gamma_d^5\Lambda_\Sigma
 >4\left(\frac4{11}\right)^5\frac{79Q}{160}
 =\frac{10112}{805255}Q
 >\frac Q{100},
\tag{41}
\]
and
\[
 4\gamma_d\Lambda_{\mathscr A_{\rm int}}
 >4\left(\frac4{11}\right)\frac{13Q}{800}
 =\frac{13Q}{550}
 >\frac Q{100}.
\tag{42}
\]
Because \(G<Q/100\), the degree-saturated core cannot occur through stage \(5\) for \(q^\Sigma\), nor through stage \(1\) for \(q^{\mathscr A_{\rm int}}\). Therefore there are nested full-dimensional cap bodies or positive same-base reweightings
\[
 C=C_0^\Sigma\supseteq C_1^\Sigma
 \supseteq\cdots\supseteq C_6^\Sigma,
 \qquad
 q_j^\Sigma=\gamma_d^j q^\Sigma,
\tag{43}
\]
\[
 C=C_0^{\rm int}\supseteq C_1^{\rm int}
 \supseteq C_2^{\rm int},
 \qquad
 q_j^{\rm int}=\gamma_d^j q^{\mathscr A_{\rm int}},
\tag{44}
\]
with unchanged edge supports and
\[
 W(C_j^\Sigma)\geq4\gamma_d^j\Lambda_\Sigma,
 \qquad
 W(C_j^{\rm int})\geq
 4\gamma_d^j\Lambda_{\mathscr A_{\rm int}}.
\tag{45}
\]
Equations (12)--(45) account for every full or rescaled auxiliary label, every charged original-parent midpoint, every same-parity pooled-anchor midpoint, every collision, and every source capacity. They do not identify any residual rank in (33)--(35) with the quotient-lattice rank or energy of a common-midpoint dyadic star, and the cap bodies in (43)--(44) inherit matching weights but not the original common-midpoint KKT stress. No terminal-star or full weak-Oertel conclusion is asserted.
